---

<Layout
  title="Word Hunt Cheat Guide: Fair Ways to Find More Words"
  description="Solve your GamePigeon Word Hunt board, then learn the prefixes, suffixes, and short words that help you score more on your own."
  path="/guides/word-hunt-cheat"
  schema={schema}
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-12 pt-6 sm:pt-8">
    <header id="top" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-xs text-brand-400 dark:text-brand-300"><a href="/" class="hover:text-headline">Home</a> / <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-headline">Guides</a> / <span aria-current="page">Word Hunt Cheat Guide</span></nav>
<h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-headline dark:text-headline-dark sm:text-4xl">Word Hunt Cheat Guide: Fair Ways to Find More Words</h1>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-400 dark:text-brand-300">By <a href="/about" class="hover:text-headline">Word Hunt Solver</a> · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-06">October 6, 2026</time></p>
<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Solve your board, then learn the patterns behind every word.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-5 text-left"><WordHuntSolver client:load /></div>
<section id="is-using-a-word-hunt-solver-cheating" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Is Using a Word Hunt Solver Cheating?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">It depends on when you use it. A solver is fair when you use it to learn, and unfair when you use it to beat a friend who thinks you're playing on your own.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">When Using a Solver Is Unfair</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Word Hunt is a match between you and a friend in iMessage. If you look up words during that match and your friend doesn't know, you get help they don't have. That's cheating, even if it's only one round.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Fair Ways to Use a Solver</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Use it after a round to see <a href="/" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">every word you missed</a>. Use it on <a href="/evolver" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">Board Evolver practice boards</a>. Or agree with a friend that you'll both use one, which turns the match into a speed contest. In each case, everyone knows the rules.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="how-do-people-cheat-at-word-hunt" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">How Do People Cheat at Word Hunt?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Most people searching how to cheat on Word Hunt want one of two things: a list of answers for their current board, or a tool that plays for them. Here's how each works and why neither helps you improve.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Looking Up Words Mid Round</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Some players type their board into a solver while the round is running and copy the longest words. The catch is that rounds are short and timed, so time spent switching apps is time you're not swiping.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Why the Timer Makes Lookups Hard</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Typing 16 letters, reading a results list, and then tracing each path takes real time. No word hunt hack removes that delay. Learning a few strong patterns lets you find words without leaving the game.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Auto Solvers and Bots</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">A Word Hunt auto solver is a program that reads the board from the screen and swipes words for you. Several hobby versions exist online. They take the game out of your hands, and you learn nothing from them. We don't build them or link to them.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="cheat-sheet" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Word Hunt Cheat Sheet: Letter Patterns to Look For</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">This cheat sheet works without any tool. Word Hunt only counts word length, so patterns that make words longer are worth learning first.</p>
<img src="/images/word-hunt-prefix-suffix.webp" alt="Short words growing into longer ones with prefixes and suffixes, like UN plus TIE making UNTIE and STAR plus ED making STARED" width="1200" height="700" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="mt-4 h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 dark:border-brand-700" />
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Common Prefixes</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Look for RE, UN, DE, and PRE in front of a word you've found. TIE becomes UNTIE, and RUN becomes RERUN, when those letters touch the start of the path.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Common Suffixes</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Check the end of each word for S, ED, ER, ING, and TION. One base word can turn into four or five longer ones. STAR can become STARS, STARE, STARED, and STARES.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Letter Pairs That Start Many Words</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">TH, ST, CH, and SH begin many English words. When you see two of these letters touching, start your scan there and follow the vowels next to them.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">4</span><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Patterns That Waste Your Time</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Some spots on a board rarely pay off. A clump of consonants with no vowel touching it seldom makes a word. A Q with no U next to it usually leads nowhere in English. And a word with a double letter, like BOOK, needs two separate O tiles that touch, since you can't use one tile twice. Spot these fast and move on.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="words-for-word-hunt-short-words-that-add-up" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 2v6h6M16 13H8M16 17H8"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Words for Word Hunt: Short Words That Add Up</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">When people look for the best words for Word Hunt, short common words are a good place to start, since you can swipe them in a second. This isn't a full word hunt word list. These picks are checked against the ENABLE word list our solver uses, and they're built from common letters like E, A, R, T, N, S, O, and I.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Useful 3 Letter Words</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">ANT, ARE, ART, ATE, EAR, EAT, ERA, NET, ONE, ORE, RAN, RAT, SAT, SEA, SET, SIT, TAN, TAR, TEA, TEN, TIE, TIN, TOE, and TON.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Useful 4 Letter Words</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">EARN, EAST, NOTE, RAIN, RATE, RENT, REST, RIOT, ROSE, SEAT, SENT, STAR, TEAR, TIDE, TILE, TIME, TONE, TIRE, and TORE.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Useful 5 Letter Words</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">ALERT, ALTER, IRATE, NOTES, RAINS, RATES, SNARE, STARE, STONE, TEARS, TONES, and TRAIN. Notice how many of these are short words with one letter added. That's a pattern worth looking for.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Plurals and Word Endings</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Every time you find a noun or verb, check for an S next to its last letter. TONE can become TONES, TONED, and STONE if the letters connect. Each new form counts as its own word.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="manual-word-hunting-vs-using-a-solver" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M12 3v18M5 7h14M5 7l-3 7a4 4 0 0 0 6 0L5 7zM19 7l-3 7a4 4 0 0 0 6 0l-3-7z"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Manual Word Hunting vs Using a Solver</h2></div>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 shadow-sm dark:border-brand-700"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead class="bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold"></th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Hunting on your own</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Using a solver</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-brand-100 dark:divide-brand-700"><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Fair in a real match</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Only if your friend agrees</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Builds your skill</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes, if you review the results after a round</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Finds every word</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes, every word in its word list</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Works under time pressure</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Slow to switch back and forth</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">You can use both: play on your own, then check the board afterward.</p>
</section>
<section id="how-to-find-more-words-without-a-solver" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">How to Find More Words Without a Solver</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Start in the center of the board, where each tile has the most neighbors. Grab every 3 letter word you see without stopping. Then go back to your best base words and try adding letters to the front and back. Our <a href="/guides/word-hunt-tips" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">Word Hunt strategy guide</a> covers this in depth.</p>
</section>
<section id="frequently-asked-questions" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M9.1 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.8 1c0 2-3 3-3 3M12 17h.01"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div>
<div class="card mt-3 !p-5"><p class="flex items-start gap-3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span>Do Cheat Sheets work on 5x5 Boards?</span></p><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 pl-10">Yes. The same prefixes, suffixes, and short words work on any size. A 5x5 board has 25 tiles instead of 16, so there are more paths and usually more words to find.</p></div>
<div class="card mt-3 !p-5"><p class="flex items-start gap-3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span>Will the Game accept every Word on this List?</span></p><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 pl-10">Not always. Our lists come from the ENABLE word list, and <a href="/#rejected-words" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">GamePigeon's word list</a> is a different one that hasn't been made public. Because that list isn't public, we can't say which words it leaves out.</p></div>
</section>
<aside class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-brand-50 p-5 dark:bg-brand-800/60" aria-label="Related guides"><p class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"><span class="text-headline dark:text-headline-dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20V3H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 0 4 5.5v14z"/><path d="M6.5 17A2.5 2.5 0 0 0 4 19.5 2.5 2.5 0 0 0 6.5 22H20v-5"/></svg></span>Related Guides</p><div class="mt-3 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><a href="/guides/word-hunt-tips" class="card group flex items-start gap-3 !p-5 transition hover:border-headline"><span class="text-headline dark:text-headline-dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span><span><span class="block font-bold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-headline dark:text-white">Word Hunt strategy guide</span><span class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">scanning routines and real solved boards</span></span></a><a href="/guides/word-hunt-solver-vs-word-finder" class="card group flex items-start gap-3 !p-5 transition hover:border-headline"><span class="text-headline dark:text-headline-dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span><span><span class="block font-bold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-headline dark:text-white">Word tool comparison</span><span class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">which tool fits which puzzle</span></span></a></div></aside>
<section id="sources" class="scroll-mt-24 py-6">
<div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-10 w-10 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.5.5l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7-7l-1.7 1.7"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.5-.5l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7 7l1.7-1.7"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Sources</h2></div>
